From: SkorionOS packaging maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] drm: preserve automatic panel orientation on kmscon 10.0

Port the original honjow panel-orientation/plane-reset patch to 10.0.4.
The renderer now owns one display from construction onward: combine its
panel correction with --rotate before backend initialization and font
sizing, and do not reapply it on font changes. Grab keys already pass an
effective orientation. Reset optional primary-plane rotation on every
atomic commit, preserving the legacy path and propagating add failures.

Keep all four kernel enum-name mappings from the original patch; fbdev
and missing/unknown properties retain normal orientation. Extend the
upstream renderer test to exercise every panel/user combination, backend
fallback, geometry before set, and rotation across repeated font setup.

diff --git a/src/render/text.c b/src/render/text.c
--- a/src/render/text.c
+++ b/src/render/text.c
@@ -176,6 +176,13 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Since 10.0 the display belongs to this renderer for its whole lifetime.
+	 * Apply the panel correction once, before backend init and font sizing.
+	 * Font changes and VT refreshes must not reapply it, and grab-key rotation
+	 * continues to operate on the effective orientation returned by get(). */
+	text->orientation = (enum Orientation)(((unsigned int)text->orientation +
+			(unsigned int)display_get_panel_orientation(disp)) % 4);
+
 	ret = new_text(text, backend);
 	if (ret) {
 		if (backend)
@@ -386,6 +393,10 @@
  */
 int kmscon_text_rotate(struct kmscon_text *txt, enum Orientation orientation)
 {
+	if (!txt)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	/* Callers pass an effective orientation, including the panel correction. */
 	if (txt->ops->rotate)
 		return txt->ops->rotate(txt, orientation);
 	return 0;
